for a lot of us the cancellation of  silent Hills last year felt like a stake  to the heart pt 2 ps4 exclusive  precursor offered a tantalizing glimpse  into what Hideo Kojima creator of the  Metal Gear series and guillermo del toro  renowned film director were capable of  when pairing together even though silent  Hills is dead that doesn't mean the duo  has permanently parted ways at this  year's dice awards a pair will give the  keynote address titled a conversation  with hideo kojima in Guillermo del Toro  according to the event organisers the  pair will share insight into their  respective creative visions and  processes Jeff kelia games media veteran  who organizes the game awards will  moderate the discussion this  conversation will revisit some of their  fondest memories from their own  individual careers as well as some of  the pivotal moments from each other's  work that remain a constant source of  inspiration in addition Kojima will be  inducted into the academy of interactive  arts and sciences Hall of Fame at the  event later this month Padilla and ultra  have said they are interested in working  together on something new where no  collaborations have been officially  announced the 18th annual dice awards  will take place on februari 18th and if  anything comes out of it stay tuned to  gamespot com for all the latest info
 

